On  ftp://ftp2.compaq.com/pub/linux/RedHat/7.2-alpha/updates/ is a
2.4.18 update kernel which fixes several vulnerabilities

=09https://rhn.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2003-025.html

The updated kernel comes with some new features.  These new
features are not officially supported at this time but should work.  This
includes but is not limited to:

        DAC960 cards:
               See attachment.

        AlphaServer 2100A (AS2100A), a.k.a Lynx systems.

        DS25 systems.

        ES47 & ES80 systems:
        These systems don't have a system serial port, but do have an fir=
mware
        console interface. To use this interface as the console, specify
        "console=3Dsrm" on the kernel command line.

=09srm_settings (kernel boot parameter):
               See attachment.

        DRM/DRI:
                The default DRM is from XFree86 4.3.0. In most cases, thi=
s works with the
                4.1.0 XFree86 provided. There are some problematic cases =
(such as the
                Radeon 7000) where the old DRM is still needed with this =
X server. The
                "old"  DRM modules are still provided with a -4.1.0 appen=
ded to their name.
                These can be selected with aliases in /etc/modules.conf. =
For example, if you
                have a Radeon 7000 and have trouble with 3D apps with the=
 default DRM, you
                can select the old DRM by adding this line to /etc/module=
s.conf:

                alias radeon radeon-4.1.0

        kernel-milo rpm:
                Once again the kernel start address had to move to make r=
oom for a larger
                SRM console. The new kernel start address overlaps the ad=
dress range that
                MILO was moved to when room had to be made for an 8MB con=
sole footprint.
                The kernel-milo package is built with legacy start addres=
s which should
                work on all MILO systems. To reduce it's footprint even m=
ore, support for
