Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit
Content-Disposition: attachment; filename="relnotes-srm_settings.txt"

30 April 2003

For numerous platforms based on APECS, CIA, or PYXIS core logic, clean
shutdown and automatic reboot have been impossible using 2.4.x Linux
kernels.

By adding "srm_settings" to the boot command line options, the SRM
console settings for PCI resources will be maintained by the Linux
kernel, thus allowing proper function of the shutdown and reboot
operations.

The platforms are:

APECS
-----
AS200/250/255/300/400
AlphaPC64 (Cabriolet)

CIA
---

EB164
AlphaPC164
AS500 (MAVERICK and BRET)
AS600 (ALCOR)
AS600A (ALCOR PRIMO)
AS800 (CORELLE)
AS1000A (NORITAKE)

PYXIS
-----

MIATA
AlphaPC164-LX
AlphaPC164-SX

