Well, I'm having lots of fun attempting to install RedHat 7.2 on my Multia.....

In order to try to eliminate various factors I'm trying to do a network install as my attempts to install via CD have failed and I suspect that the CDs I've burnt are not being read correctly on my RRD43.

I've set up an nfs filesystem on anther Linux box and exported it. I boot the Multia up, select an nfs install, input all the necessary IP addresses and attempt to connect. From the nfs server I see a brief connect to port 111 which immediately goes into SYN_RECEIVE and that's about it. Eventually the attempt times out on the Multia. I've also tried an FTP install to about the same effect. 

I've turned off all iptables firewalling, tested the NFS and FTP from another system and it's all OK. I can also ping the multia on the IP address I gave it.

Now, one point of interest, I couldn't get the network to function using twisted pair, so it's currently connected via an AUI cable and a very nice Digital AUI to TP converter (DETPM). Next stage is to dig up a SCSI disk and copy the installation CDs onto it but this will be more of a pain.....


Huw Davies
