Hmm; we did test all the network install options.

IIRC, I had to use "noprobe" mode on the Multia, so that I could load
the DE4X5 driver instead of the TULIP, for use with twisted pair. The
TULIP driver just wouldn't work for me on that box. Note that this
isn't something new, I believe it's always had trouble on several of
our boxes - Multia and AS250 come quickly to mind.

> Now, one point of interest, I couldn't get the network to function
> using twisted pair, so it's currently connected via an AUI cable and
> a very nice Digital AUI to TP converter (DETPM). Next stage is to
> dig up a SCSI disk and copy the installation CDs onto it but this
> will be more of a pain.....

Try using the DE4X5 driver with twisted pair; I had success that way.

Good luck.

