I think answer is simple.

There's no point keep manufacturing/stocking EOL'd model specific
parts(costs too much to keep inventory) but vendor will still
carry a generic parts since it is not model specific and can be
used among several(many) other machines as long as standard(spec)
matches.

PC100 ECC Unbuffered is still out there.
I know some chip vendor quit making these chips, but you should
not have a problem getting these parts.

You DON'T really have to use 164LX specific memory.


