>> you are Apple and then you can get folks to pay $2K and under.:)]
> UNDER $1000??
> Even a Dell desktop workstation costs more than that..
> Under $2500 is maybe a bit more reasonable.

I'm not talking about reality hear, but expectations.
The MARKET defines a desktop machine as being under $1,000.
You can walk up to any 10 people (who have a clue) who will swear that 
they can buy the fastest Intel based top of the line gaming rig for 
less than $1,000. (Those without a clue will say $500 to $10,000.)

But since they have never bothered to try to buy one, they have no clue 
what the cost of a real system is.

There are a couple of geeks who realize that they will pay $2500-4000 
for a system, but they are few and far between.

Just look at today's newspapers (at least in phila) -- HPQ is selling a 
512 meg P4 laptop for $1199. And everyone knows that a laptop costs 
about twice as much as a desktop. (I think the ads are a typo because 
they offer two systems with radically different performance 
characteristics for the same $1199 price! -- EVO N800v 1.8GHz P4 and 
EVO N1020v 2.4GHz. ... www.hp.com/go/phl/ or your favorite reseller.)

> Apple and the G5 is not likely to be the solution you are looking for.
